{"baseRefOid":"8df5cf5b9e5558333c12ce0f2867551c357a42fe","body":"Owners need a reviewed path to move lasting memory between Hermes and LifeOS. They also need a complete software removal option that retains personal data and recovery records.\n\nThis change adds authenticated import, portable export, provider return, and complete software removal. Version 0.6.0 remains an unpublished candidate.\n\n- Import preserves each source occurrence, original bytes, references, and provenance.\n- The owner selects every import and export decision. Current owner, source, destination, and capacity checks apply before publication.\n- Provider return drains writers, selects reviewed built-in memory, and replaces the LifeOS prompt through a recovery journal.\n- Complete removal requires a verified provider return and separate owner review. It selects qualified stock Hermes and disables Discord.\n- The retained password-authenticated command can resume removal or restore software. Software restoration preserves later built-in memory.\n- Data-only backups exclude runtime workspaces. Complete guest backups retain the standalone recovery files and software copies.\n\nValidation:\n\n- The independent package review is clear at b35cf86e. The primary repeats all 55 closure controls with clean diagnostics.\n- The earlier 52db archive passes 991 integration tests with unchanged archive sources.\n- The corrected b35 archive passes 716 native Hermes tests and 33 user interface component tests.\n- The owner browser imports authorized .213 source files, replays the portable bundle, and preserves existing references at revision 1.\n- Real private FlashNext sessions save a new native fact, recall it in a separate session, and recall it through built-in Hermes after verified return.\n- The candidate 0.6.0 archive passes 716 native Hermes tests. Its complete integration run continues.\n\nRemaining release gates:\n\n- [ ] Normal installed complete removal and fresh stock model behavior.\n- [ ] Stock guest reboot and retained standalone recovery.\n- [ ] Actual wrong-password refusal, software rollback, and preservation of later built-in learning.\n- [ ] Installed worker interruption and authenticated recovery.\n- [ ] Final exact-package qualification and release evidence.\n\nDevelopment .252 and daily .253 remain on qualified 0.5.0. This pull request does not import, reset, or change daily data.\n\nThe contract is in docs/memory-portability.md. Detailed measured evidence and open gates are in docs/verification/2026-10-15-memory-portability/.\n","headRefOid":"c86b5887b899ca779afbb217c33843e1ee12c381","isDraft":true,"number":29,"title":"feat(memory): add portability and software removal","url":"https://github.com/0ut5ider/lifeos-hermes-plugin/pull/29"}
